 "script": {
  "intro": "This is every robot I've met, from 2013 to 2025. I found most of them at Expo 2020 and GITEX in Dubai, and the first two I built myself.",
  "outro": "Six robots in twelve years, and I'm still meeting new ones. Thanks for watching, and tell me which one you'd most like to meet.",
  "lines": [
   "That same month, Expo 2020 was a city of its own, with robots around every corner.",
   "There I met a driverless police car, the M02, built in the UAE to patrol narrow streets at up to fifteen kilometres an hour.",
   "October 2022, back at GITEX with over a hundred and seventy thousand visitors, and first up, a robot misting disinfectant as it glided through the crowd.",
   "Pepper was everywhere, greeting people. SoftBank built it to read emotions in faces and voices, and made about twenty-seven thousand before pausing production in 2021.",
   "And then Ameca, with the most expressive robot face I've ever seen. Britain's Engineered Arts unveiled it in 2021, and I met it again in 2025.",
   "In 2023 a robot waiter parked itself beside our table in Dubai, trays stacked like a little trolley, no tips required.",
   "In August 2025, a Promobot was greeting visitors in a company lobby. Promobot's robots work in about forty countries, including at the Dubai Mall."
  ],
